# Review is enforced by identity, not by convention (D260921.3-P).
#
# GitHub refuses to let an author approve their own pull request. That is the
# whole mechanism: agents implement as the machine account, so they cannot
# approve their own work, and approval has to come from this account. With one
# shared identity there was nothing here to enforce - every agent was the owner.
#
# Consequence to know: a PR opened BY @chris-egan cannot be approved by
# @chris-egan either. Work is meant to arrive from the machine lane; a PR
# raised from this account needs a second reviewer or an admin merge.
* @chris-egan
